      "updated": 1786129183089,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1) Why MCP instead of function calling?\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1) Why MCP instead of function calling?\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "v0CLS665ead8amp74HKti",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 35.5804999128498,
      "y": 1590.6101097045248,
      "width": 852.6712036132812,
      "height": 80,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a6",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 630645197,
      "version": 486,
      "versionNonce": 1419188963,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786129180327,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Function calling describes how a model express its intent to invoke a function.\n- MCP standardize how capabilities are discovered and invoked across independently developed tool providers\n- MCP give consistent boundary for tools, schema, resources, discovery, transports, server ownership\n- MCP prevent agent runtime being tight couple to certain service (SOT) ",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Function calling describes how a model express its intent to invoke a function.\n- MCP standardize how capabilities are discovered and invoked across independently developed tool providers\n- MCP give consistent boundary for tools, schema, resources, discovery, transports, server ownership\n- MCP prevent agent runtime being tight couple to certain service (SOT) ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
